  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nFor the following test example : \n[  def test_new_subgroups_with_group_param(self):\n](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/torch/testing/_internal/distributed/distributed_test.py#L924)            # Initialize global test environment\n            self._init_global_test()\n            # Set up GPU devices for each rank\n            init_multigpu_helper(dist.get_world_size(), BACKEND)\n            # Create two subgroups: one with ranks [0,2] and another with ranks [1,3]\n            cur_subgroup, subgroups = dist.new_subgroups_by_enumeration(\n                ranks_per_subgroup_list=[[0, 2], [1, 3]]\n            )\n\n\nAs you can see the [0, 2] [1,3] was hard-coded, expecting the test to be world size of 4. \nHowever, recent enablement of 8B200 runner failed while running this unit test, e.g. https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/actions/runs/16764647752/job/47468897556 \nClearly, the world size was 8. \nDoes the use of this macro guarantee the world size is 4, looks like no from the above failure. \n\n### Versions\n\nmain\n\ncc @H-Huang @awgu @wanchaol @fegin @fduwjj @wz337 @wconstab @d4l3k @pragupta @seemethere @malfet @pytorch/pytorch-dev-infra",
